        "original_id": "94fde1ad-1386-5f9e-a1f9-d0a70ffb991d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Pago Pago, Tafuna, Tutuila, American Samoa, Hoonah, Alaska, Nu'uuli\n- Airports: Pago Pago International Airport, Tafuna Airport, Hoonah Airport\n- Codes: IATA PPG, ICAO NSTU, FAA LID PPG, IATA HNH, ICAO PAOH, FAA LID HNH\n- Topics: airport location\n\nFacts:\n- Pago Pago International Airport, also known as Tafuna Airport, is a public airport in Tafuna on Tutuila in American Samoa, an unincorporated territory of the United States.\n- Pago Pago International Airport has the codes IATA PPG, ICAO NSTU, and FAA LID PPG.\n- Pago Pago International Airport is 7 miles southwest of the central business district of Pago Pago.\n- Hoonah Airport is a state-owned public-use airport in Hoonah, Alaska.\n- Hoonah Airport has the codes IATA HNH, ICAO PAOH, and FAA LID HNH.\n- Hoonah Airport is 1 nautical mile southeast of the central business district of Hoonah.\n- Tafuna is on a peninsula 1 mile north of Pago Pago International Airport and 1 mile south of Nu'uuli, American Samoa.",
